  <content>
  <section>
    <para dir="ltr">The equation \(g(t) = 2 + 23.7t - 4.9t^2\) models the height, in meters, of a pumpkin \(t\) seconds after it has been launched from a catapult. Which of the following substitutions into the quadratic formula is correct to find the value of \(t\) where the pumpkin hit the ground?</para>
  </section>
</content>
</document>
